class.description:
Builds a pathfinding graph from the cells of a [TileMapLayer] and returns paths as cells or as local positions. Neighbors follow the tile shape, layout, offset axis and coordinate system of the [TileSet]; costs and blocked cells come from custom data layers named in [member options], or from [method _get_cell_cost] and [method _is_cell_blocked].
Two backends are used, chosen from the [TileSet] (see [enum Backend]): [AStarGrid2D] for square and diamond isometric maps, [AStar2D] for stacked and stairs isometric, half-offset square and hexagon maps.
The graph covers the used rect of the layer ([method get_region]). Blocked cells stay in the graph as solid or disabled points, so changing them is cheap. The layer has no per-cell change signal: call [method update_cells] after changing cells and [method update_all] after larger changes or a change of [member options].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var graph = TileMapPathGraph.create($Ground)
var cells = graph.get_cell_path(Vector2i(0, 0), Vector2i(10, 4))
var points = graph.get_point_path(Vector2i(0, 0), Vector2i(10, 4))

$Ground.set_cell(Vector2i(5, 2), 0, Vector2i(1, 0))
graph.update_cells([Vector2i(5, 2)])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var ground = GetNode<TileMapLayer>("Ground");
var graph = TileMapPathGraph.Create(ground);
var cells = graph.GetCellPath(new Vector2I(0, 0), new Vector2I(10, 4));
var points = graph.GetPointPath(new Vector2I(0, 0), new Vector2I(10, 4));

ground.SetCell(new Vector2I(5, 2), 0, new Vector2I(1, 0));
graph.UpdateCells([new Vector2I(5, 2)]);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Not thread-safe, like [AStar2D]: build and query on one thread. The graph backend uses several times the memory of the grid backend per cell; prefer square or diamond isometric maps for very large maps on the Web and mobile.
